§ ANTI-PATTERNS (token-wasteful)
  ✗ long compound paths w/o aliasing
    sys.subsystem.component.subcomponent.property → 9+ tokens
    ✓ alias sc = sys.subsystem.component; sc.subcomponent.property
  
  ✗ excessive comments
    # this is a comment about what the next line does → 12 tokens waste
    ✓ only annotate non-obvious intent
  
  ✗ repeated full paths
    ✓ define once, reference by short name or $0/$1/$2
  
  ✗ unicode decorative glyphs (★ ♦ ⚡) for aesthetics
    ✓ ASCII aliases → same semantics, fewer tokens
  
  ✗ mixing unicode + ASCII for same glyph in one document
    ✓ pick one mode per document, stay consistent
  
  ✗ restating header content in first sentence of block
    ✓ header IS the statement; body provides detail

§ DECISION PROCEDURE (which form to use)
  1. check BPE cost of unicode glyph
  2. if cost ≤ 2 tokens ∧ freq ≥ medium → unicode acceptable
  3. if cost ≥ 3 tokens → W! use ASCII alias
  4. if target = CSLv3 compiler → ASCII (parser simplicity)
  5. if target = spec for Apocky → unicode OK where ≤ 2 tokens
  6. if target = agent CoT → ASCII preferred (max density)
  7. if target = cross-Hydra handoff → ASCII (portability)

§ CONTINUOUS MEASUREMENT
  W! measure per-glyph BPE cost quarterly
  W! prune glyphs where cost > semantic-value
  R! maintain ROI table: ROI = (freq × bits) / token-cost
  R! new glyph added → must justify ROI > 1.5 before adoption
QED
